{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":227709,"duration_api_ms":143263,"num_turns":22,"result":"The fix is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n**Root cause:** `_extract_text_from_json()` in `sw-loop.sh` only handled JSON arrays (`[`) in Case 2 (the jq-powered path). When Claude outputs a JSON object (`{`), the code fell through to Case 3, which emits \"JSON output but jq not available\" — even when jq is fully functional.\n\n**Fix:** Extended Case 2 to handle both JSON arrays and objects when jq is available:\n- Arrays: extract `.result` from last element, fall back to `.content` \n- Objects: extract `.result` directly, fall back to `.content`\n- Case 3 now only triggers when jq is genuinely absent\n\n**Tests added** (3 new assertions in `sw-loop-test.sh`):\n- JSON object with `.result` field extracts correctly\n- JSON object with `.content` field extracts correctly  \n- No spurious \"jq not available\" warning emitted for JSON objects\n\nAll 68 loop tests pass. The pre-existing `sw-cost-test.sh` failure is unrelated to this change.\n\nLOOP_COMPLETE","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2141a2b8-fd6d-4710-b7f2-430b292cdd49","total_cost_usd":0.7620769,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":54992,"cache_read_input_tokens":1567133,"output_tokens":5225,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":54992,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-4-6":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":5225,"cacheReadInputTokens":1567133,"cacheCreationInputTokens":54992,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7548069000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6090,"outputTokens":236,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00727,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32